> write a cover letter for this job :  o lead this transformation, we are looking for a
> Director, Global Power System Transformation (f/m/d)
> Full-time or part-time (min. 32 hours) | Strong preference for candidates based in one of Agora’s or RAP’s hubs (Washington D.C., Netherlands, Berlin, Brussels, Bangkok, Beijing, New Delhi) with option to work remotely | Frequent international travel required.
> Your responsibilities include
> As a member of the senior leadership team, you will:
> Shape the organisation’s strategy for the global power programme, with accountability for analytical quality, regional reach, and policy relevance across the techno-economics of power system transformation, grids and flexible electrification, and power market design and regulation.
> Line manage an international team across Europe, Asia, the United States and other target regions.
> Lead the programme’s analytical agenda, spanning power system pathways from fossil to clean generation, system integration of variable renewables, flexibility and storage, coal and gas transition frameworks, power markets and tariff design, grid planning and operation at transmission and distribution levels, technical connection standards, distributed energy resources (DER) integration, and stability and resilience of power systems with very high shares of renewables.
> Shape practical international and regional cooperation on power system transformation, working closely with a wide range of partners from civil society, academia, system operators, regulators, policymakers and the business sector.
> Guarantee the organisation’s programmatic coherence on power system transformation across all geographies through active coordination and knowledge sharing with regional programmes, ensuring the programme’s work stays connected to the operational realities of power system transformation on the ground.
> Represent the organisation’s global power programme to governments, regulators, utilities, funders, and think tank partners at global and national levels.
> Manage research quality, publication output, and stakeholder communication on the global stage, including expert positioning and media relations.
> Build and manage the programme’s budget, identify new funding opportunities, and develop funder relationships in support of the expanded programme.
> We are looking for
> At least 15 years of relevant professional experience, including several years of management experience in an international setting with team leadership across multiple geographies.
> Strong strategic leadership on power system transformation, from techno-economics to market design and regulation, with deep expertise in at least three major areas of the power transition.
> Understanding of how power sector policy interacts with development, energy security and affordability objectives, and ability to engage credibly with policymakers, regulators and utilities across multiple regional contexts.
> Familiarity with global power system transformation platforms and initiatives, such as G-PST, RETA, and CEM.
> Familiarity with political processes and understanding of how political decision-makers think; ability to develop and represent complex and nuanced positions across diverse institutional contexts, and proven ability to turn technical and economic analysis into policy influence.
> Collaborative leadership style appropriate for a think tank: setting direction while respecting research autonomy.
> Motivating personality who can inspire systemic, integrative thinking and work effectively across geographies and institutional cultures.
> Strong and diverse international network spanning policymakers, regulators, utilities, development finance institutions, and civil society.
> Meaningful networks globally and in at least one major region.
> Fluent written and spoken English; other language skills valued, particularly Mandarin, Korean, Japanese, Turkish, Spanish, or Southeast Asian languages.
> Willingness and ability to travel frequently to target countries and multilateral forum locations.
> 
> We assume there are excellent candidates for this role who do not meet all criteria listed above. Maybe you have certain skills we have not thought of yet? Tell us why you are the right person for this job.
> What we offer
> A high-impact senior leadership role in a mission-driven international organisation at the frontier of global power system transformation policy.
> A diverse, international working environment with flat communication and decision-making hierarchies.
> Access to offices in Berlin, Brussels, Bangkok, or Beijing with hybrid options and good digital facilities to work in one of Agora’s or RAP’s hubs worldwide.
> Flexible working hours and vacation entitlement above statutory requirements.
> Professional development, a health & wellness package depending on the country of employment and access to mental health and coaching support.
> Permanent employment contract.
> Competitive salary.
> Support with visa and work permit applications if required.
> How to apply
> We look forward to receiving your application until 31 August 2026 via the website.
> 
